Day 28: Fix a Broken MLflow Project and Re-Run It
Overview
The xFusionCorp Industries ML platform team packaged their training runs as MLflow Projects to enable reproducible execution via a single mlflow run command.

During lab startup, an automated run was executed against the project staged at /root/code/trainer/ and failed. The initial run failed because the MLproject descriptor command line was improperly configured: it forwarded an incorrectly named flag (--n_est) and omitted several required parameters (--max_depth, --test_size, --random_seed) defined in train.py.

This task involved updating /root/code/trainer/MLproject, verifying parameter passing to train.py, and executing two successful end-to-end MLflow project runs while preserving the original failed run for diagnostic tracking.

Objectives
Diagnose Initial Failure: Confirm that the initial automated run failed due to misaligned parameter flags between MLproject and train.py. Do not delete the original FAILED run.

Fix MLproject:

Align entry point arguments with train.py.

Ensure all declared parameters (n_estimators, max_depth, test_size, random_seed) forward to train.py using authoritative flag names (--n_estimators, --max_depth, --test_size, --random_seed).

Execute Project Runs:

Run 1 (Default values): Execute mlflow run . -e train --env-manager=local using default parameters.

Run 2 (Parameter Overrides): Execute mlflow run . -e train -P n_estimators=200 -P max_depth=10 --env-manager=local to pass explicit overrides.

Verification:

Confirm that the trainer experiment records two FINISHED runs alongside the original FAILED run.

Validate parameter logging in MLflow UI across default and overridden runs.

Technical Details & Files
Location: /root/code/trainer/

Files:

MLproject: MLflow project descriptor defining entry points, parameters, and command execution.

train.py: Trainer script using argparse to parse --n_estimators, --max_depth, --test_size, and --random_seed (must not be modified).

Step-by-Step Implementation Guide
Step 1: Inspect the Project Files
Inspect the train.py argument parsing requirements and the initial MLproject definition:

Bash
cd /root/code/trainer
cat train.py
cat MLproject
Initial MLproject Defect:
The command: key was invoking python train.py --n_est {n_estimators}, which used an invalid flag name and omitted --max_depth, --test_size, and --random_seed.

Step 2: Fix the MLproject Configuration
Update /root/code/trainer/MLproject to pass all declared parameters with their exact argparse flag names:

YAML
name: trainer

entry_points:
  train:
    parameters:
      n_estimators:
        type: int
        default: 100
      max_depth:
        type: int
        default: 5
      test_size:
        type: float
        default: 0.2
      random_seed:
        type: int
        default: 42
    command: "python train.py --n_estimators {n_estimators} --max_depth {max_depth} --test_size {test_size} --random_seed {random_seed}"
Step 3: Execute MLflow Runs
Run the updated MLflow project entry point twice using --env-manager=local:

1. Run with Default Parameters
Bash
mlflow run . -e train --env-manager=local
Output: Succeeded with n_estimators=100, max_depth=5 (Run ID: b57bb2b57e7c457397a04bec27ae08f9).

2. Run with Parameter Overrides
Bash
mlflow run . -e train -P n_estimators=200 -P max_depth=10 --env-manager=local
Output: Succeeded with n_estimators=200, max_depth=10 (Run ID: 4a1bc785213c4511a475b14d088ff242).

Verification & Results
MLflow UI Check:

Access the MLflow UI at http://localhost:5000/#/experiments/1.

The trainer experiment contains:

1 original FAILED run from startup (preserved for diagnosis).

2 successful FINISHED runs.

Parameter Log Verification:

Default Run (b57bb2b57e7c457397a04bec27ae08f9): params.n_estimators = 100, params.max_depth = 5, params.test_size = 0.2, params.random_seed = 42.

Override Run (4a1bc785213c4511a475b14d088ff242): params.n_estimators = 200, params.max_depth = 10, params.test_size = 0.2, params.random_seed = 42.
